docker-compose.yml your PostgreSQL container name is iys_postgres, user is iys_user, and database is iys_db.

Here are the ways to check the tables in your database:

Option 1: Quick Command (One-liner)
Run this directly in your terminal (PowerShell / Command Prompt):

powershell
1) docker exec -it iys_postgres psql -U iys_user -d iys_db -c "\dt"
Tip: If your tables are under custom schemas (not just public), 
2) run: docker exec -it iys_postgres psql -U iys_user -d iys_db -c "\dt *.*"

Option 2: Interactive psql Shell
If you want to stay in the PostgreSQL console to inspect schema, columns, or run queries:

Enter the PostgreSQL shell:

powershell
3) docker exec -it iys_postgres psql -U iys_user -d iys_db
List all tables:

sql
\dt
(or \dt+ for table sizes and descriptions)

Inspect a specific table structure (e.g., users):

sql
\d users
Query Flyway migration history (since Flyway manages your schema):

sql
SELECT installed_rank, version, description, success FROM flyway_schema_history;
Exit the shell:

sql
\q
